### Summary of Changes

1. **Safety Try-Catch Blocks in [atCommandProcessor.ts](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/large_triaged_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_25972/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/cli/src/ui/hooks/atCommandProcessor.ts)**:
   - Wrapped the looping mechanism in `checkPermissions` with try-catch blocks to gracefully ignore unresolvable mock/alias reference paths during permission evaluation.
   - Wrapped the individual iterations in `resolveFilePaths` with a try-catch to elegantly skip any glob search or statistical processing errors, such as checking non-existent path-like module aliases like `@/lib/formatTimeRange`.
   - If path resolution fails, unhandled exceptions are caught and skipped, safely falling back to treating the literal `@`-prefixed text normally as query content directed to the LLM.

2. **Test Implementation in [atCommandProcessor.test.ts](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/large_triaged_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_25972/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/cli/src/ui/hooks/atCommandProcessor.test.ts)**:
   - Added a dedicated unit test scenario: `"should gracefully handle unresolvable @ paths like "@/lib/formatTimeRange" and fall back to treating them as literal text without throwing"`. This test passes a prompt query containing `@/lib/formatTimeRange` and verifies that `handleAtCommand` successfully processes it and returns the original text without throwing any errors or crashing.
   - Incorporated a lightweight global `File` polyfill in both `atCommandProcessor.test.ts` and [test-setup.ts](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/large_triaged_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_25972/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/cli/test-setup.ts), alongside a Node-18 preloading polyfill script `preload.cjs`, resolving potential test environment limitations cleanly.

